# Global Rules (.windsurfrules)

## Backend (Java Spring Boot) - Hexagonal Architecture (Strict)
- The backend MUST follow strict Hexagonal Architecture (Ports & Adapters).
- Domain layer MUST NOT depend on framework/infrastructure.
- Only adapters may depend on Spring, persistence, web, messaging, etc.
- All external interactions MUST be expressed as ports (interfaces) and implemented by adapters.
- Use cases (application services) orchestrate domain behavior and call ports.

## Frontend (React) - Zero Trust
- The frontend MUST be treated as untrusted.
- The backend MUST recalculate and validate all monetary amounts (totals, subtotals, taxes/discounts if any).
- Backend MUST validate stock, prices, and business rules independently of any frontend-provided values.

## Security
- Authentication MUST be JWT Stateless.
- Do NOT use server-side sessions.
- JWT validation MUST occur on every request to protected endpoints.

## CORS
- Backend MUST allow CORS only for the origin:
  - http://localhost:3000
- Allowed headers MUST include Authorization and Content-Type.
- Allowed methods MUST include GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS.
